WEBVTT

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:06.012
<v Ishita>Where are we? Everything here is made of bricks!

00:00:06.012 --> 00:00:07.929
<v Mishu>Welcome to a Harappan city!

00:00:07.829 --> 00:00:15.880
<v Mishu>The people here built their houses with bricks of a standard size, and they used weights and measures across their cities.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:19.063
<v Ishita>But how do we know that? It was so long ago.

00:00:19.063 --> 00:00:23.251
<v Mishu>Scales with marks on them have been dug up at Harappan sites.

00:00:23.251 --> 00:00:26.693
<v Ishita>Look, little stone blocks, right next to the balance!

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:29.864
<v Mishu>Here's some extra info. It may not be in your textbook.

00:00:29.764 --> 00:00:36.150
<v Mishu>Harappan weights were little stone cubes, and they were made to the same standard sizes in Harappan towns far apart.

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:38.672
<v Ishita>Why couldn't they just measure with their hands?

00:00:38.672 --> 00:00:42.228
<v Mishu>So what makes a good standard? It is a handy size.

00:00:42.128 --> 00:00:47.191
<v Mishu>It does not change with place or time. Everyone understands it the same way.

00:00:47.091 --> 00:00:51.206
<v Mishu>It does not get destroyed. And copies can be made easily.

00:00:51.206 --> 00:00:53.534
<v Mishu>Does a handspan pass? No.

00:00:53.434 --> 00:00:57.865
<v Mishu>It changes from person to person, and it grows as you grow!

00:00:57.865 --> 00:01:00.378
<v Ishita>Oh! My hand is still growing!
